# Rule: ImaginaryPartQuotient
# Before (rejected):
# forall u C,v C*:
#     C_abs(v)!=0
#     C_abs(v)^2!=0
#     img(u/v)=(img(u)*re(v)-re(u)*img(v))/C_abs(v)^2
# Former behavior: strict run success=false, phase search_proof.
# Now (verified directly):
forall u C,v C*:
    C_abs(v)!=0
    C_abs(v)^2!=0
    img(u/v)=(img(u)*re(v)-re(u)*img(v))/C_abs(v)^2

forall z C,w C*:
    C_abs(w)!=0
    C_abs(w)^2!=0
    img(z/w)=(img(z)*re(w)-re(z)*img(w))/C_abs(w)^2

# Boundary: Whole-fact WD still checks both division denominators; the imaginary numerator has subtraction, not addition.
# Gate: target/release/litex -strict -f examples/proof_nodes/equal/by_builtin_rule/complex_quotient_imaginary_coordinates.lit
# Regression: tests/unit/execute/legacy_six_simple_bt/tests.rs
